(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["intro-to-pa-profession-pa-intro-master-exam-form-b"]={"title":"Intro to PA Profession Comprehensive Master Exam — Form B","category":"Intro to PA","exam":"General","sem":"summer-1-2026","questions":[{"q":"Dr. Eugene Stead served as Chairman of Medicine at which university in the 1960s?","choices":["Emory University","University of Washington","University of Colorado","Duke University"],"answer":3,"exp":"Dr. Eugene Stead served as Chairman of Medicine at Duke University in the 1960s, where he founded the first PA program in 1965. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The concept of using medical corpsmen with 2-3 years of training as 'externs' was proposed by:","choices":["Dr. Richard Smith","Dr. Eugene Stead","Dr. Henry Silver","Dr. Charles Hudson"],"answer":3,"exp":"Dr. Charles Hudson, president of the NBME, introduced the PA 'concept' in his 1961 speech to the AMA House of Delegates, envisioning corpsmen with 2-3 years of training as technical 'externs' who would not make independent medical judgments. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The first PA program at Duke was how many years in length?","choices":["Two years","Three years","Four years","One year"],"answer":0,"exp":"The first PA program at Duke, launched in 1965 with four former Navy corpsmen, was a two-year program. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which French non-physician provider role existed in the 1800s?","choices":["Village health worker","Externe","Officer de Santé","Feldsher"],"answer":2,"exp":"The Officer de Santé was a non-physician provider role in France during the 1800s, one of the historical predecessors identified for the PA profession. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which stage of PA development is characterized by 'increased utilization outside of scope originally designed' and reimbursement obtained through Medicare?","choices":["Evaluation","Incorporation","Ideology stage","Maturation"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Incorporation stage of the five-stage model (Ideology, Implementation, Evaluation, Incorporation, Maturation) is marked by expanded utilization beyond the profession's originally designed scope and by obtaining reimbursement through Medicare. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 1970, the National Academy of Science outlined three types of PAs; which type did national medical organizations support for primary care?","choices":["Type A","Type B","Type D","Type C"],"answer":0,"exp":"Of the three PA types (A, B, C) outlined by the National Academy of Science in 1970, Type A — the broadest-trained type — was the type national medical organizations supported for primary care. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The organization now known as PAEA was originally founded in 1972 under what name?","choices":["ARC-PA","AAPA","APAP","NCCPA"],"answer":2,"exp":"The organization now known as PAEA was founded in 1972 as APAP (Association of Physician Assistant Programs), later renamed PAEA in 2005. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 1993, which agency agreed to register PAs to prescribe controlled substances?","choices":["DEA","FDA","CMS","FSMB"],"answer":0,"exp":"In 1993, the DEA agreed to register PAs to prescribe controlled substances. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Mississippi, the last state to license PAs, did so in what year?","choices":["2010","2007","2000","1997"],"answer":2,"exp":"Mississippi, the last state to license PAs, did so in 2000. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"By 2007, what milestone was reached regarding PA prescribing?","choices":["PANRE-LA officially launched","The very first CAQ was formally issued","Name change to Physician Associate","All states allowed PAs to prescribe"],"answer":3,"exp":"By 2007, all states had extended prescribing authority to PAs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The first Certificates of Added Qualifications (CAQs) were created by NCCPA in what year?","choices":["2001","2014","2011","2007"],"answer":2,"exp":"NCCPA created the first Certificates of Added Qualifications (CAQs) in 2011. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which 2010 legislation dramatically increased the need for PAs by covering an additional 20-30 million patients?","choices":["Balanced Budget Act","Affordable Care Act","Health Manpower Act","Rural Health Clinic Services Act"],"answer":1,"exp":"The 2010 Affordable Care Act dramatically increased the need for PAs by extending coverage to an additional 20-30 million patients. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Who became the first PA to travel in space (2021)?","choices":["Sally K. Ride","Hayley Arceneaux","Christina Koch","Dr. Mae Jemison"],"answer":1,"exp":"Hayley Arceneaux became the first PA to travel in space in 2021, as part of the Inspiration4 mission. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The 1977 Rural Health Clinic Services Act provided what for PAs working in rural clinics?","choices":["Automatic licensure","Free malpractice coverage","Medicare reimbursement","Loan forgiveness"],"answer":2,"exp":"The 1977 Rural Health Clinic Services Act provided Medicare reimbursement for PA services in rural clinics. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Where is the Stead Center, associated with the PA History Society, located?","choices":["Florida itself","North Carolina","Washington DC","Colorado itself"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Stead Center, associated with the PA History Society (PAHx), is located in North Carolina, reflecting Duke's foundational role in the profession's history. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Up to what fraction of ARC-PA Commissioners must be PAs?","choices":["All","Three-fourths","Two-thirds","One-half"],"answer":2,"exp":"Up to two-thirds of ARC-PA's Commissioners must be PAs, with the remainder made up of physicians, program deans, and public members. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which body accredits post-professional PA doctoral programs (PPDP)?","choices":["AAPA","NCCPA","ARC-PA","PAEA"],"answer":2,"exp":"ARC-PA accredits post-professional PA doctoral programs (PPDP), with standards that became effective in September 2025. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The mission of PAEA emphasizes advancing excellence in PA education through leadership, scholarship, equity, and:","choices":["Certification","Inclusion","Reimbursement","Advocacy"],"answer":1,"exp":"PAEA's mission emphasizes advancing excellence in PA education through leadership, scholarship, equity, and inclusion. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"NCCPA logging of CME hours must occur how often?","choices":["Every 2 years","Every 5 years","Every 10 years","Annually"],"answer":0,"exp":"NCCPA requires PAs to log CME hours every 2 years as part of certification maintenance (100 hours per cycle). — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which exam is administered by NCCPA for initial certification?","choices":["PANCE","OSCE","PACKRAT","CASPA"],"answer":0,"exp":"The PANCE (Physician Assistant National Certifying Exam) is administered by NCCPA for initial certification. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"NCCPA Code of Conduct breaches may result in all of the following EXCEPT:","choices":["Full revocation of NCCPA certification","A formal censure issued by NCCPA","Automatic license suspension by the state","An official letter of concern from NCCPA"],"answer":2,"exp":"NCCPA Code of Conduct breaches can lead to revocation of certification, formal censure, or a letter of concern, but NCCPA cannot itself automatically suspend a state license — it may only report violations to state boards, which then act independently. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Approximately how many members does the AAPA have?","choices":["330,000+","74,000+","200,000+","24,000+"],"answer":1,"exp":"The AAPA has approximately 74,000+ members. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The AAPA House of Delegates includes chapters from the 50 states, DC, US Virgin Islands, Puerto Rico, and how many uniformed services?","choices":["3","5","7","9"],"answer":1,"exp":"The AAPA House of Delegates includes chapters from the 50 states, DC, US Virgin Islands, and Puerto Rico, plus 5 uniformed services, totaling 58 chapters. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which is an AAPA commission?","choices":["The Commission on State Licensure","The Commission on Program Accreditation","Commission on the Health of the Public","The Commission on National Certification"],"answer":2,"exp":"The Commission on the Health of the Public is one of AAPA's six commissions. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"To become an Assembly of Representatives (AOR) rep, a student must be a SAAAPA member in what standing?","choices":["Honorary status","Emeritus status","Probationary","Good standing"],"answer":3,"exp":"To become an Assembly of Representatives (AOR) rep, a student must be a SAAAPA member in good standing, elected or appointed by a registered student society. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"FAPA student membership costs how much for the entire enrollment period?","choices":["$100","$195","$60","$75"],"answer":2,"exp":"FAPA student membership costs $60 for the entire enrollment period, extended 6 months post-graduation for boards. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"FAPA was established in what year?","choices":["1974","1972","2001","1965"],"answer":0,"exp":"FAPA (Florida Academy of Physician Associates), the only organization representing PAs in Florida, was established in 1974. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The Florida PA Council recommends PAs to the Governor for appointment to which body?","choices":["The national ARC-PA accreditation commission","The Florida Board of Medicine's Council on PAs","The national NCCPA Board of Directors","The national AAPA Board of Directors"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Florida PA Council recommends PAs to the Governor for appointment to the Florida Board of Medicine's Council on PAs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"PAF funds include the R.K. Pedersen Global Outreach Endowment and PA Student:","choices":["Loans","Scholarships","Malpractice funds","Grants for licensure"],"answer":1,"exp":"PAF funds include the R.K. Pedersen Global Outreach Endowment and PA student scholarships, among other philanthropic awards. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The National Medical Challenge Bowl is held annually at which meeting?","choices":["ARC-PA site visit","The PAEA educators forum","NCCPA conference","AAPA national meeting"],"answer":3,"exp":"The National Medical Challenge Bowl is held annually at the AAPA national meeting, run by the Student Academy of AAPA. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which PA competency domain includes 'demonstrate emotional resilience, stability, adaptability, and tolerance of ambiguity'?","choices":["Interpersonal and communication skills","Knowledge for practice competency domain","Person-centered care competency domain","Professionalism and ethics competency domain"],"answer":0,"exp":"'Demonstrate emotional resilience, stability, adaptability, and tolerance of ambiguity' falls under the Interpersonal and Communication Skills competency domain. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The PA competencies have been adopted and revised by how many national PA organizations?","choices":["Three","Four","Five","Two"],"answer":1,"exp":"The PA competencies have been adopted and revised by all four national PA organizations (AAPA, ARC-PA, NCCPA, PAEA), most recently in 2021. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"On the PANCE, up to what percentage of questions are legal/ethical?","choices":["2%","1%","5%","10%"],"answer":0,"exp":"On the PANCE, up to 2% of questions are legal/ethical in content. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The PANCE test day consists of six blocks of how many questions each?","choices":["90","70","50","60"],"answer":3,"exp":"The PANCE test day consists of six blocks of 60 questions each, totaling 360 questions over 6 hours. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A PANCE candidate must wait how many days after the expected graduation date to test?","choices":["30 days","14 days","3 days","7 days"],"answer":3,"exp":"A PANCE candidate must wait 7 days after the expected graduation date before testing. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"For grads on/after Jan 1, 2003, PANCE eligibility lasts up to how many years?","choices":["Five","Three","Six","Ten"],"answer":2,"exp":"For graduates on or after January 1, 2003, PANCE eligibility lasts up to six years, or six attempts, whichever comes first. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The maximum number of PANCE attempts allowed is:","choices":["Three","Four","Six","Unlimited"],"answer":2,"exp":"The maximum number of PANCE attempts allowed is six, or six years of eligibility, whichever comes first. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"In Florida, is continued NCCPA certification required to maintain licensure?","choices":["No, but 100 hrs CME every 2 yrs is required","Yes, but only for the first five years of practice","Yes, continued certification is always required","Yes, but only for maintaining prescribing privileges"],"answer":0,"exp":"In Florida, continued NCCPA certification is not required to maintain licensure, but 100 hours of CME every 2 years is required instead. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which process demonstrates the ability to perform certain tasks and procedures and is renewed annually at the institutional level?","choices":["Certification","Privileging","Licensure","Credentialing"],"answer":1,"exp":"Privileging demonstrates the ability to perform specific tasks and procedures and is renewed annually at the institutional level. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Institutional credentialing is mandated by the Joint Commission and which other body?","choices":["CMS","FSMB","NCQA","ARC-PA"],"answer":2,"exp":"Institutional credentialing is mandated by both the Joint Commission and NCQA (National Committee for Quality Assurance). — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Scope of practice is determined by Medicare regulations, federal/state laws, and:","choices":["National PA organizations","Patient preference","The supervising physician alone","Hospital bylaws and policies"],"answer":3,"exp":"Scope of practice is determined by Medicare regulations, federal/state laws, and hospital bylaws and policies. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A PA serving as a surgical first assistant is reimbursed at what rate of the primary surgeon fee?","choices":["50%","100%","13.6%","85%"],"answer":2,"exp":"A PA serving as a surgical first assistant is reimbursed at 13.6% of the primary surgeon's fee. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Since what year has Medicare allowed direct reimbursement to PAs (if state law allows)?","choices":["2022","2020","2017","2021"],"answer":0,"exp":"Since 2022, Medicare has allowed direct reimbursement to PAs, if state law allows. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which payment model uses a single payment covering all services for a condition over a defined period?","choices":["Fee-for-service","Incident-to","Capitation","Bundled payment"],"answer":3,"exp":"A bundled payment is a single payment covering all services for a condition over a defined period, such as surgery's pre-op, intra-op, and post-op care combined. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Under EMTALA, if an unstable patient is transferred, what must occur?","choices":["The PA alone signs and certifies the transfer","A physician must be consulted and sign the certificate","Nothing additional needs to occur at all","The patient alone signs a liability waiver"],"answer":1,"exp":"Under EMTALA, if an unstable patient is transferred, a physician must be consulted and must sign the transfer certificate. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Regarding documentation, an original note may be:","choices":["Deleted if incorrect","Rewritten entirely from scratch","Ignored after signing","Amended but never deleted"],"answer":3,"exp":"An original clinical note may be amended, but it should never be deleted, in order to preserve the legal record and continuity of care. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which OTP component addresses PA liability?","choices":["PAs are responsible for the care they provide","A physician is always liable for PA care","PAs are never held liable for any care they provide","Liability rests with the hospital only"],"answer":0,"exp":"One component of Optimal Team Practice states that PAs are responsible for the care they provide, and that a physician should not be liable for a PA's care unless the PA acted on the physician's specific instructions. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The Licensure Compact is best described as a(n):","choices":["Optional agreement between states easing multistate practice","A national certification examination administered by NCCPA","A shared national malpractice insurance pool","A mandatory requirement imposed by federal law"],"answer":0,"exp":"The Licensure Compact is an optional agreement between states that eases multistate PA practice by letting a PA licensed in a member state gain practice authorization in other member states more easily. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Interprofessional collaboration relies on trust, mutual respect, and:","choices":["Independence","Shared values","Hierarchy alone","Competition"],"answer":1,"exp":"Interprofessional collaboration relies on trust, mutual respect, and shared values among team members. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which nursing role monitors all aspects of labor and delivery and may provide well-woman care?","choices":["Clinical Nurse Specialist","Licensed Practical Nurse, or LPN","A CRNA, or nurse anesthetist","Certified Nurse Midwife (CNM)"],"answer":3,"exp":"The Certified Nurse Midwife (CNM) monitors all aspects of labor and delivery and may also provide well-woman care. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A Registered Dietitian Nutritionist performs which of the following?","choices":["Medical nutrition therapy","General anesthesia care","Radiologic imaging","Licensed psychotherapy services"],"answer":0,"exp":"A Registered Dietitian Nutritionist performs medical nutrition therapy. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which provider diagnoses and treats hearing and balance problems and holds a doctorate?","choices":["Optometrist","Respiratory therapist","Speech-language pathologist","Audiologist"],"answer":3,"exp":"The audiologist diagnoses and treats hearing and balance problems and holds a doctorate. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A Physical Therapist requires which level of education?","choices":["Bachelor's","Doctoral","Associate's","Master's"],"answer":1,"exp":"A Physical Therapist requires a doctoral level of education. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Occupational therapy primarily helps patients:","choices":["Deliver babies during labor and childbirth","Administer prescribed medications to patients","Interpret diagnostic laboratory test results","Perform tasks in daily living and working environments"],"answer":3,"exp":"Occupational therapy primarily helps patients perform tasks in daily living and working environments. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"The healthcare system has shifted from a physician-centered model to one that includes:","choices":["Administrator perspectives","Patient/family perspectives","Health insurer perspectives","Regulator perspectives"],"answer":1,"exp":"The healthcare system has shifted from a physician-centered model to one that includes patient/family perspectives. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A respiratory therapist assumes primary responsibility for:","choices":["Chronic wound care management","Pharmacy medication dispensing","All respiratory care treatments","Direct surgical assisting duties"],"answer":2,"exp":"A respiratory therapist assumes primary responsibility for all respiratory care treatments. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which is a primary-care specialty field?","choices":["Internal medicine","Radiology","Cardiothoracic surgery","Dermatology"],"answer":0,"exp":"Internal medicine is a primary-care specialty field, alongside family medicine and pediatrics. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"A growing hospital-based role for PAs described in the clinical practice lecture is:","choices":["Independent surgery","Locum radiology","Solo anesthesia","Hospitalist practice"],"answer":3,"exp":"Hospitalist practice is described as a growing hospital-based role for PAs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"Per PAEA, professionalism is described as one of the top 10 what?","choices":["Licensing requirements","Cognitive skill sets","Clinical procedures","Noncognitive attributes"],"answer":3,"exp":"Per PAEA, professionalism is described as one of the top 10 noncognitive attributes valued in PA students and practitioners. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professionalism"},{"q":"The AAPA annual CME conference provides members with which key opportunity?","choices":["Networking and continuing education","National certification testing","Formal program accreditation","State licensure renewal process"],"answer":0,"exp":"The AAPA annual CME conference provides members with networking and continuing education opportunities. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"}]};
